{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376312-thought-on-using-resonant-and-dissonant-keywords-with-multi-material-artifacts","id":1376312,"title":"Thought on using Resonant and Dissonant keywords with multi-material artifacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-23T14:43:51-07:00","id":1376312,"title":"Thought on using Resonant and Dissonant keywords with multi-material artifacts","content":"I'm right now writing Evocations for one of my players' suit of armor, which is made primarily of black jade but includes some moonsilver thread. As I was thinking about Resonant and Dissonant effects for those, I thought about how the interplay of two materials can direct the story told by the Evocations (in this case, the Evocations taking up the mantle of a jade-scaled sea monster) and thought &quot;Wouldn't it be interesting if there were Resonant effects for multiple materials for a single Charm?&quot;<br /> <br /> For example, suppose there's a power bow composed of equal parts soulsteel and starmetal. It could have an Evocation that gains an effect if the wielder is resonant with soulsteel, a different effect if the wielder is resonant with starmetal, and a Solar could gain both. Likewise, there could be an Evocation that loses one effect if the wielder is dissonant with soulsteel, a different effect changes if the wielder is dissonant with starmetal, and a Solar avoids both.<br /> <br /> Such artifacts would almost certainly be created for Solars, strange Exigents, and maybe Alchemicals once we hear more about those. If someone were particularly ambitious, such an approach could be applied to a five-metal artifact, so that any non-Solar using it effectively wields a very different weapon from any other type of Exalt that took it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T17:41:52-07:00","id":1376339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376312-thought-on-using-resonant-and-dissonant-keywords-with-multi-material-artifacts#post1376312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm right now writing Evocations for one of my players' suit of armor, which is made primarily of black jade but includes some moonsilver thread. As I was thinking about Resonant and Dissonant effects for those, I thought about how the interplay of two materials can direct the story told by the Evocations (in this case, the Evocations taking up the mantle of a jade-scaled sea monster) and thought &quot;Wouldn't it be interesting if there were Resonant effects for multiple materials for a single Charm?&quot;<br /> <br /> For example, suppose there's a power bow composed of equal parts soulsteel and starmetal. It could have an Evocation that gains an effect if the wielder is resonant with soulsteel, a different effect if the wielder is resonant with starmetal, and a Solar could gain both. Likewise, there could be an Evocation that loses one effect if the wielder is dissonant with soulsteel, a different effect changes if the wielder is dissonant with starmetal, and a Solar avoids both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that sounds pretty solid to me. I do like the idea that a single Artifact might have different facets to explore for alternative wielders. <br /> <br /> I would personally think that in a case where there are several Resonances that the mixture of materials should be more dramatic than being at the fringes.<br /> <br /> I <b>do</b> have a reservation about the possibilities of Solars getting access to multiple effects simultaneously, on grounds of things like being overpowered, overloaded or just plain feeling worth more per dot than other Artifacts. I think that part of the idea could use some workshopping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such artifacts would almost certainly be created for Solars, strange Exigents, and maybe Alchemicals once we hear more about those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can also imagine scenarios in which the crafter deliberately set out to create an Artifact that would show different sides to different Exalted, or where the focus was less on the potential wielders and more about realising a certain vision for the Artifact itself. I think that really goes for some of the example Artifacts, where the creator was struck by inspiration from some particular scenario or the materials they had to work with and wanted to capture that in jade or moonsilver.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T10:04:53-07:00","id":1376410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376312-thought-on-using-resonant-and-dissonant-keywords-with-multi-material-artifacts?p=1376339#post1376339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <b>do</b> have a reservation about the possibilities of Solars getting access to multiple effects simultaneously, on grounds of things like being overpowered, overloaded or just plain feeling worth more per dot than other Artifacts. I think that part of the idea could use some workshopping.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always the option of &quot;Choose only one Resonant bonus if multiple are available&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can also imagine scenarios in which the crafter deliberately set out to create an Artifact that would show different sides to different Exalted, or where the focus was less on the potential wielders and more about realising a certain vision for the Artifact itself. I think that really goes for some of the example Artifacts, where the creator was struck by inspiration from some particular scenario or the materials they had to work with and wanted to capture that in jade or moonsilver. </div> </div> </div>Good ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T18:01:44-07:00","id":1377250,"title":"","content":"An idea I had once was for an artifact that was constructed from a tree branch taken from a particularly mutable part of the Caul, treated with Moonsilver and bound with Jade, and turned into a Wrackstaff. Base power is that it can be planted to grow fruit and firewood like a traveler\u2019s staff, but I was thinking that it could create two evocation trees. One based on the solidity of Jade and boosting attacks against Fae, removing mutations, and stabilizing Wyld areas. The other would be based around mutations and healing, using the fruit as a vector. Both trees would be full of the Dissonant keyword, so that the charms of one tree are going to be less effective than the other.<br /> <br /> The benefit for mastering both trees would be that you can perform a ritual which, if successful, would grant you the Caul\u2019s permission to make the pilgrimage, regardless of who controls what cities. It wouldn\u2019t protect you from, say, being eaten by a Lunar on the way or whatever, but it would ensure that the rituals themselves wouldn\u2019t kill you and that the pilgrimage would succeed, if you managed to complete it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T18:09:47-07:00","id":1377252,"title":"","content":"I also made this thing: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14CJAfJXUuzIZrONFNB0cTqAMtHtWSXC80LNzxF1Kl7E\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...XC80LNzxF1Kl7E</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T22:16:02-07:00","id":1377284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376312-thought-on-using-resonant-and-dissonant-keywords-with-multi-material-artifacts?p=1377250#post1377250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both trees would be full of the Dissonant keyword, so that the charms of one tree are going to be less effective than the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, Lunars aren't Dissonant with Jade (excepting when they enter warform), and Dragon-Blooded aren't Dissonant with Moonsilver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T08:26:00-07:00","id":1377347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376312-thought-on-using-resonant-and-dissonant-keywords-with-multi-material-artifacts?p=1377250#post1377250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea I had once was for an artifact that was constructed from a tree branch taken from a particularly mutable part of the Caul, treated with Moonsilver and bound with Jade, and turned into a Wrackstaff. Base power is that it can be planted to grow fruit and firewood like a traveler\u2019s staff, but I was thinking that it could create two evocation trees. One based on the solidity of Jade and boosting attacks against Fae, removing mutations, and stabilizing Wyld areas. The other would be based around mutations and healing, using the fruit as a vector. Both trees would be full of the Dissonant keyword, so that the charms of one tree are going to be less effective than the other.<br /> <br /> The benefit for mastering both trees would be that you can perform a ritual which, if successful, would grant you the Caul\u2019s permission to make the pilgrimage, regardless of who controls what cities. It wouldn\u2019t protect you from, say, being eaten by a Lunar on the way or whatever, but it would ensure that the rituals themselves wouldn\u2019t kill you and that the pilgrimage would succeed, if you managed to complete it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who would have constructed this artifact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T11:22:58-07:00","id":1377766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376312-thought-on-using-resonant-and-dissonant-keywords-with-multi-material-artifacts?p=1377284#post1377284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, Lunars aren't Dissonant with Jade (excepting when they enter warform), and Dragon-Blooded aren't Dissonant with Moonsilver.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok, good point. Then there should be a Resonant bonus to each charm. The point here is that one tree should be less effective for each group that might want it, giving them reasons to not want to take it or even pretend it doesn\u2019t exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T11:27:02-07:00","id":1377767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376312-thought-on-using-resonant-and-dissonant-keywords-with-multi-material-artifacts?p=1377347#post1377347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who would have constructed this artifact?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that both the Realm and the Lunar host have legends of it being made by them and stolen by the other group, but that it was actually made during the original taming of the Caul by both a Lunar and a Dragon-Blooded working together.<br /> <br /> Thinking on it, possibly the capstone evocation should grant full resonance with all the evocations on the artifact, in addition to allowing the Caul pilgrimage ritual. That way you still get something even if you\u2019re not interested in the Caul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:26:22-07:00","id":1377845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376312-thought-on-using-resonant-and-dissonant-keywords-with-multi-material-artifacts?p=1377767#post1377767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking that both the Realm and the Lunar host have legends of it being made by them and stolen by the other group, but that it was actually made during the original taming of the Caul by both a Lunar and a Dragon-Blooded working together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as long as the story doesn\u2019t finish with them getting stuck in a canyon together, and a Solar convincing the Dragon-Blooded and Lunars alike that he remembers the <i>true</i> history, and that the whole conflict was just a game they were playing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}